Author: Brandon Kimball
Description: 
  K_IDE.py is a python-based code-editor that uses the Gnome-Toolkit(3) bindings for GUI elements. 
  It was built for a specific system with limited available dependencies and permissions, but to provide quick spawning of terminals to test code in the desired language.
  Given the above, it is very limited in what is can do and what it was intended to do, and likely will not be updated any further.

The version for Python 2.7 is still available and functional.
v0.3b is for Python 3, it is not functional and was just a quick ctrl+f proof-of-concept.
